# MAGIC The automation is a configuration-driven Excel reporting engine for Broadridge FY26 risk assessment analytics. It uses pandas to validate and prepare source data and openpyxl to populate and format a workbook template. The process is executed for each configured account group and produces a repeatable set of summary and analysis schedules.
# MAGIC Input data must include the configured account-group field, group field, account field, four balance-period columns, and three fluctuation columns. Numeric fields are converted to numeric values, invalid or blank numeric values are replaced with zero, and the resulting population is grouped in source order for reporting.
# MAGIC The summary schedule presents account-level detail by group, group subtotals, grand totals, and an account-level comparison to materiality. The analysis schedule presents configured current-versus-prior comparison tables, materiality multiples by period, and optional charts. Materiality, performance materiality, and CTT are displayed from the central configuration block.
# MAGIC The workbook template is copied or repurposed according to the configured template-sheet names and output-sheet titles. The automation applies standardized fonts, borders, number formats, row grouping, hidden detail rows, worksheet headers, and chart formatting.
